  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @brief Processing function for the Q31 IIR lattice filter.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *S points to an instance of the Q31 IIR lattice structure.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the block of output data.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @param[in] blockSize number of samples to process.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * @details
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * \par
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * The function is implemented using an internal 64-bit accumulator.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * The accumulator has a 2.62 format and maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplicatio
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator result overflows it wraps around rather than clip.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by 2*log2(numStages)
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  * After all multiply-accumulates are performed, the 2.62 accumulator is saturated to 1.32 format a
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_iir_lattice_q31.c ****  */
